 "title": "How Tollgate works, with its three feedback loops",
 "desc": "An isometric scene. You ask in plain words. The AI writes a plan, and fresh AIs review it; when they find problems, it goes back to the plan. The tests are written and locked before any code. The AI builds in its own copy of the project. At the gate, the tests and reviewers check each try: below 70%, it goes back and the AI tries again from its best try; after 3 tries, the advisor decides; at 70% or more, the barrier lifts and the change goes into main. After the task, up to 3 lessons become rules for the next one. A dot shows one change travelling: it fails once, then passes.",
